{
  "source": "Blackfrosch/VAGEDCSuite",
  "source_url": "https://github.com/Blackfrosch/VAGEDCSuite",
  "license_note": "No explicit license declared in upstream repo. Patterns extracted from C# source for interoperability with the ECU-organizer parser; refer to the original repo for terms before redistribution.",
  "extraction_notes": [
    "The VAGEDCSuite C# code identifies VAG-flashed EDC15/EDC16/EDC17 firmware images by scanning the bin for ASCII/byte markers and then verifying the surrounding partnumber bytes (Bosch 10-digit '0281xxxxxx' and VAG 11-char e.g. '038906018A').",
    "The dominant marker across every EDC15/EDC16/EDC17 parser is the ASCII literal 'EDC  ' (0x45 0x44 0x43 0x20 0x20) which precedes the Bosch and VAG partnumber blocks.",
    "EDC17 firmwares are additionally identified by 'EDC17_', 'EDC17_CPx4' (Audi), 'EDC17_CPx2' (BMW), 'EDC17_C06' (BMW), 'ME(D)/EDC17', or by the literal 'EDC17  ' (with two trailing spaces) in 512 KiB Audi Q7 3.0 TDI images.",
    "AT/MT codeblock detection inside an EDC15 image uses the ASCII suffixes 'EDC  AG' (automatic) and 'EDC  SG' (manual transmission).",
    "Non-ASCII byte runs (SVBL/codeblock signatures, MAP/MAF switch) are EDC15-family specific and are how the tool locates the start of mapping tables — they are useful as secondary VAG-EDC15 confirmation when the ASCII partnumber block is encrypted or scrambled.",
    "File-size heuristics: 2 MiB (2*1024*1024) implies EDC17, 512 KiB (0x80000) implies EDC15V/P, 1 MiB (0x100000) is also accepted for EDC15. The MSA15/MSA6 checksum search hard-requires 0x80000.",
    "Rules below are byte-for-byte transcriptions of the C# `findSequence` calls; the 'mask' field mirrors the C# wildcard-mask array (1=match, 0=wildcard).",
    "EDC17 parser applies `reverseEndian` BEFORE pattern search (LL LL AXIS AXIS MAPDATA is big-endian), so signatures listed as 'apply_after_endian_swap: true' must be matched on the byte-swapped buffer."
  ],
  "ecu_type_strings_seen_in_partNumberConverter": [
    "EDC15C",
    "EDC15M",
    "EDC15P",
    "EDC15P-6",
    "EDC15V-5.1",
